# Changes and Improvements

## Generic Types
The class can now handle different types of custom data (e.g., Integer, Double, Long, Float), not just String or String[].

## Asynchronous Methods
Asynchronous methods have been added for reading and writing custom data.

## Logging
Logging has been added to facilitate monitoring and debugging of changes in custom data.

## Improved Documentation
Comments and documentation of the methods have been improved to provide more details about their functionality and usage.

## Future Improvements
Consider adding more custom events, more data types, and additional optimizations based on your plugin's needs.

### Constructor

```java
public PlayerData(JavaPlugin plugin) {
    this.plugin = plugin;
}
```
The constructor initializes the PlayerData instance with a reference to the JavaPlugin. This reference is used to create NamespacedKey objects and to log messages.

### Setting Custom Data

```java
public void setCustomData(Player player, String dataKey, String[] values) {
    NamespacedKey key = new NamespacedKey(plugin, dataKey);
    String combined = String.join(",", values);  // Serializing the array into a single string
    player.getPersistentDataContainer().set(key, PersistentDataType.STRING, combined);

    // Logging the data change
    plugin.getLogger().log(Level.INFO, "Set custom data for player " + player.getName() + " with key " + dataKey);

    // Triggering the custom event to notify about the data change
    PlayerDataChangedEvent dataChangedEvent = new PlayerDataChangedEvent(player, dataKey, values);
    Bukkit.getServer().getPluginManager().callEvent(dataChangedEvent);
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey, String[] values
Description: Sets custom data for a player using a key and an array of strings. The array is serialized into a single comma-separated string and stored. After setting the data, it logs the action and triggers a custom PlayerDataChangedEvent.

### Getting Custom Data

```java
public String[] getCustomData(Player player, String dataKey) {
    NamespacedKey key = new NamespacedKey(plugin, dataKey);
    String value = player.getPersistentDataContainer().get(key, PersistentDataType.STRING);
    return value != null ? value.split(",") : new String[0];  // Deserializing the string back into an array
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Retrieves custom data for a player using a key. The stored string is deserialized back into an array of strings.

### Asynchronous Getting Custom Data

```java
public CompletableFuture<String[]> getCustomDataAsync(Player player, String dataKey) {
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> getCustomData(player, dataKey));
} 
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Asynchronously retrieves custom data for a player using a key. Returns a CompletableFuture that resolves to an array of strings.

### Getting String Data

```java
public String getStringData(Player player, String dataKey) {
    NamespacedKey key = new NamespacedKey(plugin, dataKey);
    return player.getPersistentDataContainer().get(key, PersistentDataType.STRING);
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Retrieves a single string value of custom data for a player using a key.

### Asynchronous Getting String Data

```java
public CompletableFuture<String> getStringDataAsync(Player player, String dataKey) {
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> getStringData(player, dataKey));
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Asynchronously retrieves a single string value of custom data for a player using a key. Returns a CompletableFuture that resolves to a string.

### Checking Custom Data

```java
public boolean hasCustomData(Player player, String dataKey) {
    NamespacedKey key = new NamespacedKey(plugin, dataKey);
    return player.getPersistentDataContainer().has(key, PersistentDataType.STRING);
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Checks if a player has custom data associated with a given key.

### Asynchronous Checking Custom Data

```java
public CompletableFuture<Boolean> hasCustomDataAsync(Player player, String dataKey) {
    return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> hasCustomData(player, dataKey));
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Asynchronously checks if a player has custom data associated with a given key. Returns a CompletableFuture that resolves to a boolean.

### Removing Custom Data

```java
public void removeCustomData(Player player, String dataKey) {
    NamespacedKey key = new NamespacedKey(plugin, dataKey);
    player.getPersistentDataContainer().remove(key);

    // Logging the data removal
    plugin.getLogger().log(Level.INFO, "Removed custom data for player " + player.getName() + " with key " + dataKey);
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Removes custom data associated with a given key from a player and logs the action.

### Asynchronous Removing Custom Data

```java
public CompletableFuture<Void> removeCustomDataAsync(Player player, String dataKey) {
    return CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> removeCustomData(player, dataKey));
}
```
Parameters: Player player, String dataKey
Description: Asynchronously removes custom data associated with a given key from a player. Returns a CompletableFuture that completes when the data has been removed.

